I have carefully checked all the proofs provided in the appendix. The core idea generally follows that of (Wang et al., 2022), and there is no major issues. However, I still have the following concerns: (1) In line 748-752, a constant factor $2$ appears suddenly in terms $\mathbb{E} _{p(x,y^{
eg} _{ ar{x}})}  [f(x)^{	op}  \mu _{ ar{x}}]$ and $\sqrt{\mathbb{E} _{p(x,y^{
eg} _{ ar{x}})}  [\Vert f(x)^{	op}  \mu _{ ar{x}} \Vert^2] }$. It's not clear to me why this constant factor appears. It seems that maintaining the original factor $1$ does not effect the final bounds. Besides, inequality (4) holds only when $\mathbb{E} _{p(x,y^{
eg} _{ ar{x}})}  [f(x)^{	op}  \mu _{ ar{x}}] \geq 0$. The authors should provide more detailed explanation on this. (2) In line 902-904, the authors claim that inequality (3) could be obtained by $\Vert f(x) - \mu _{y _{ ar{x}}} \Vert^2 = \Vert f(x) \Vert^2 + \Vert \mu _{y _{ ar{x}}} \Vert^2 -2 f(x)^	op \mu _{y _{ ar{x}}} \leq \epsilon^2_q$ and $\Vert f(x) \Vert \leq 1$. However, I can only conclude that $-2 f(x)^	op \mu _{y _{ ar{x}}} \leq \epsilon^2_q - (\Vert f(x) \Vert^2 + \Vert \mu _{y _{ ar{x}}} \Vert^2)$ holds. Moreover, if $\Vert f(x) \Vert \geq 1$ and $\Vert \mu _{y _{ ar{x}}} \Vert \geq 1$ hold, I can also conclude that $-2 f(x)^	op \mu _{y _{ ar{x}}} \leq \epsilon^2_q - 2$. But, inequality (3) holds only when $-2 f(x)^	op \mu _{y _{ ar{x}}} \geq \epsilon^2_q - 2 $ holds. (3) In line 910-915, there is no appearance of the term $ rac{1}{2} \epsilon^2_q$, yet it appears in line 923-925. Could the authors clarify this?

